WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.320
Useful work often needs more than a fresh chat.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.820
ChatGPT has features for related work,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.240
for documents, and for data.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.570
We'll try them with invented material.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.190
And if a feature is missing on your plan,

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.070
each lesson gives you a plain text alternative.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.200
Start with the job, not the buttons.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.440
Our invented office needs a visitor checklist from a few

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.100
short notes. Keep the notes beside the draft,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.260
so every step traces back to something the office actually

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.580
supplied.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.710
A project keeps chats, files and instructions together.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.770
If it's available, create a Builder practice project.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.320
Add instructions for short New Zealand emails,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.720
with unknown details left visible.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.060
Keep the practice private, and review who has access

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.760
before you ever share real work.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.010
The notes say a visitor signs in, meets the host,

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.470
and gets a safety briefing.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.630
They don't say who gives the briefing.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.710
So that stays an open question.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.970
A checklist that invents responsibility isn't complete.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.007
Next, numbers. Upload our small jobs CSV,

00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:13.784
or paste the three rows.

00:01:13.804 --> 00:01:17.909
Ask for the total quoted value, the total accepted value,

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:20.700
and the ratio between them.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.698
Quoted comes to thirty-seven thousand dollars.

00:01:23.718 --> 00:01:25.609
Accepted, twenty-nine thousand.

00:01:25.629 --> 00:01:28.417
That's about seventy-eight point four percent.

00:01:28.437 --> 00:01:30.710
Check the sums yourself.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.320
Before you ask, pin down the question and the unit.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.420
Counting jobs is different from adding values.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.320
And if a chart appears, check its title and labels.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.450
Because that number describes accepted value.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.590
It doesn't tell you how many jobs were won,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.470
or whether any of them made money.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.370
A correct sum can still answer the wrong question.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.520
Uploads and analysis are limited on Free,

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.420
so pasting the rows as text is fine.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.190
For writing, ChatGPT may put a draft in a writing block

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.790
that you can edit directly.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.470
If you don't see one, just ask for revisions in the chat.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.430
Ask for one change, like clearer headings,

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.890
then compare it with the notes again.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.800
Memory can use relevant preferences,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.440
when it's turned on.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.840
Connected apps can bring in work sources,

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.100
when they're available and approved.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.700
Different features, different settings.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.480
Review the permissions, and open the original source.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.070
You don't need to connect your business drive to finish

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.970
this course. Use our fictional procedure and data.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.060
Try one feature, ask one clear question,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.500
and check the result.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.760
Then write a short handover note:

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.100
the source you used, what you checked,

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.180
and what's still uncertain.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.530
Give the reviewer the original material alongside the

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.410
draft. That's the habit worth keeping.
